<title>UK: TBI says in talks to buy Coventry airport.</title>
<headline>TBI says in talks to buy Coventry airport.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property company TBI Plc said on Wednesday it was in advanced discussions to buy Coventry Airport from Coventry City Council.</p>
<p>The company noted that delivery company Parcelforce earlier on Wednesday said it would invest 100 million pounds at a site near the airport to develop a parcel distribution centre.</p>
<p>&quot;Parcelforce will be the largest user of Coventry Airport and has worked closely with TBI and Coventry City Council in reaching its decision to invest in the site,&quot; TBI said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
